From 8454c72e5edb5e9edb2a8884b8333dce4f7a501c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ARRRRNY <ahmettok@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 22:30:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add an external activate-endpoint trigger for the
 running app

The app's notification-click jump had no external trigger: no CLI or socket
route could switch the running client shell to another saved machine's pane,
because `herdr --machine <label> tab focus` only moves the remote server's
state. Add `herdr app focus [--machine <label-or-id>] (--pane|--tab|--workspace)`
with a `client.activate_endpoint` API method and an `endpoint.activate.v1`
client-shell control that mirrors the notification-click jump. Without a
running shell that accepts the request the command keeps today's server-side
focus through the `--machine` bridge and reports which path it took.

